  recipeId: resistor
  concept: "Authored objective: LOAD Resistor Current ~2.46 mA.\nAuthored requirement:
    Current through the 1 kohm LOAD branch in parallel with the BOTTOM resistor.
    current \u2265 2.2 mA. current \u2264 2.8 mA. Connection pair R_LOAD_Input and
    R_LOAD_Output. Conduction required.\nGeneral teaching principle: Resistance,
    voltage and current are linked by Ohm's law for ideal resistors, while power
    dissipation needs separate evaluation.\nOnly fresh, authoritative game evidence
    can establish that this objective is complete."
  analogy: A flow restriction can suggest resistance; unlike a pipe, a resistor follows
    electrical laws.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: Current and resistor power cannot be established without voltage/current
    evidence and component values.
